  "before": "Both service-construction orders fail initial saved-track restore in r89. Both fail the forced stale-Qt-cache next-input control in r92.",
  "after": "Saved exact native external-track IDs wait for the associated tracks. Automatic attachment restore defers selection to the current media preset; explicit attachment Save still selects its default. Target-media lookup avoids using the preceding cached input.",
  "testSetup": "The initial r93 full run retains one failed production-order row, although isolated rows pass. r94 waits for Default restore to finish before manual capture and asserts actual native category delay/FPS before save; production code is unchanged from r93. The full r94 run passes all 23 functions.",
  "ordinary": "Save Finnish external track with -0.375s category delay and 30fps. Duplicate name retains draft/error; renamed retry succeeds. Default resets delay/FPS; named reapply and cold restart restore values and track. Next media uses its own episode-two attachment. Three ordinary runs exit normally with 602 modules, unchanged guards and no diagnostics.",
  "naming": "Before control fails the production popup viewport bound. After reflow correction, editor plus Cancel/Save fit normal, short, 150% and 200% component layouts with focus retained. Actual ordinary popup shows all three without further scrolling; typed draft Cancel preserves selected preset and paused clock.",
  "startupObservation": "Earlier occluded first captures are retained. In r96, explicit target-window activation followed by the initial capture shows the Finnish caption at unchanged paused 0.08s without Play/seek; this qualifies that ordinary run, not every startup configuration.",
  "limits": [
    "Supplied-state layouts do not establish Windows OS DPI acceptance.",
    "Readable-but-undecodable attachment feedback/retry and the designed online flow remain open.",
    "Native fixture and ordinary GUI have separate identities; no complete W1/W2/visual/final-package/beta acceptance."
  ]
}
